  "id": "DrugBank_DB01042 - MONDO_16093",
  "verbalization": "Melphalan, a chemotherapy agent, is linked to Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary through a chain of indications involving Altretamine. The evidence suggests that Melphalan is used in the treatment of various ovarian tumors, including Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary, and Immature Ovarian Teratoma, all of which are classified under the broader category of ovarian tumors. Altretamine, a chemotherapy drug, is indicated for all these conditions, indicating a shared therapeutic use. The presence of a common indication chain between Melphalan and Altretamine, followed by Altretamine's indication for Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary, suggests a potential mechanistic or therapeutic relationship. The integration of these paths highlights a possible pathway where Melphalan, through its use in treating related ovarian tumors, may influence the development or progression of Borderline Epithelial Tumor Of Ovary. The evidence supports a link between Melphalan and this tumor type, likely through its role in the treatment of precursor conditions, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
